ra2-modern-hezbollah-name = Hezbollah
ra2-modern-hezbollah-description = Fictional RTS faction: few veteran fighters, cheap rocket volleys and FPV micro-drone teams.
    Includes economy, production, land, air, naval and support buildings.
    New local development roster; balance and final art approval pending.

levant-r2hzrifle-name = Line Fighter
levant-r2hzrifle-description = Veteran rifle infantry, fewer and stronger: leaves the barracks Veteran, promotes quickly and takes less damage on rough ground. Conceals while stationary; moving, firing or taking damage reveals it. Detectors and splash defeat it.

levant-r2hzat-name = Ridge Missile Team
levant-r2hzat-description = Veteran ambush team with a basic shoulder-fired rocket. Conceals while stationary; a signal post or spotter improves range and reload. Vulnerable to infantry, detectors and air attacks.

levant-r2hzspotter-name = Field Spotter
levant-r2hzspotter-description = Veteran reconnaissance specialist who detects cloaked units, guides nearby missile teams, rocket vehicles and FPV teams, and relays the FPV drone link. A weak weapon makes escorts essential.
levant-r2hzfpv-name = FPV Team
levant-r2hzfpv-description = Veteran drone team that launches three one-way FPV micro-drones at targets in range and regrows one every few seconds. Strong against infantry and light vehicles. Drones crash outside the team's link; anti-air and small arms shoot them down, and killing the team downs them.
levant-r2hzquad-name = FPV Drone

levant-r2hzscout-name = Cedar Scout
levant-r2hzscout-description = The faction's hero: one concealed scout who leaves the barracks Elite, with a suppressed carbine and demolition ability. Firing or damage breaks concealment. Vulnerable once detected.

levant-r2hztechnical-name = Cedar Technical
levant-r2hztechnical-description = Fast and inexpensive machine-gun vehicle. Strong against exposed infantry, weak against armor and air attacks.

levant-r2hzrecoilless-name = Recoilless Technical
levant-r2hzrecoilless-description = Inexpensive mobile anti-armor fire on a fragile chassis. Signal coverage improves range and reload. Infantry and aircraft punish exposed vehicles.

levant-r2hzescort-name = Escort Gun Truck
levant-r2hzescort-description = Fragile mobile anti-air escort. Its ground fire discourages infantry; tanks and artillery counter it.

levant-r2hzrockets-name = Mobile Rocket Battery
levant-r2hzrockets-description = Rocket artillery: a volley of eight unguided rockets with wide scatter, a minimum range and a slow reload. Must stop to set up its stabilized firing cycle. Spotters or signal posts improve range and reload; close attacks force withdrawal.
levant-r2hzrail-name = Rail Technical
levant-r2hzrail-description = Inexpensive rocket pickup: four unguided rockets with scatter, a minimum range and a slow reload; no radar needed. Spotters or signal posts improve range and reload. Fragile up close.

levant-r2hzdrone-name = Loiter Drone
levant-r2hzdrone-description = Light one-way airborne attack that consumes the drone. Scout the target first. Anti-air fire destroys it before impact.

levant-r2hzmissileboat-name = Coastal Missile Boat
levant-r2hzmissileboat-description = Light missile craft firing three-missile salvos. Coverage from a scout boat supports coordinated fire; poor armor demands spacing and an escort.

levant-r2hzskiff-name = Attack Skiff
levant-r2hzskiff-description = Inexpensive one-way attack boat. Requires a reachable water target and is consumed on impact. Patrol screens and concentrated fire counter it.

levant-r2hzsurvey-name = Coastal Survey Boat
levant-r2hzsurvey-description = Light patrol and reconnaissance craft with sonar and fleet guidance. Prioritize its sensors; heavy warships outgun it.

levant-r2hzbunker-name = Concealed Bunker
levant-r2hzbunker-description = Stationary concealed machine-gun defense. Firing or taking damage reveals it. Detection and artillery counter the position.

levant-r2hzaanest-name = Short-Range AA Nest
levant-r2hzaanest-description = Low-cost anti-air emplacement. Cannot substitute for armor defense. Artillery attacks outside its range.

levant-r2hzcoastal-name = Coastal Missile Emplacement
levant-r2hzcoastal-description = Concealed missile defense firing four-missile salvos at ground vehicles and ships. Minimum range leaves a close-attack window. Detection and infantry counter it.

levant-r2hzrelay-name = Signal Post
levant-r2hzrelay-description = Powered six-cell support, FPV drone link and five-cell cloak detection. Eligible guided units gain range and reload bonuses; bonuses do not stack.
levant-r2hzworkshop-name = Field Workshop
levant-r2hzworkshop-description = Powered four-cell repair zone for eligible vehicles. Repairs two health per second only below 70% health. Bonuses do not stack; protect this unarmed structure.
